1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Nxd4 5. Qxd4 Ne7 6. Bd3 {... Mr. Gibson
opened with the Scotch game, and at the 12th move fell into a trap by which he
lost the Queen for two minor pieces. Nothing daunted he proceeded with the
attack; but at the 28th move Mr. Newbolt sacrificed his Queen with profit to
himself and ruin to White’s attack. After some desultory warfare for 15 more
moves Mr. Gibson resigned.} 0-1

