1. d4 d5 2. c4 {... The first game between Messrs. Crump and Allen was a
closely contested Queen’s Gambit, of a bookish nature, in which an identical
position on both sides was reached at the 8th move. It would require very
accurate analysis to pronounce on the merits of the position at the 23rd move,
when Mr. Crump made an unfortunate slip and was mated off-hand.} 0-1

